; claude: the games' rules, played without drawing them: each test
; plays a game headlessly, calling its update frame after frame with
; keys held, and checks the model (a car's laps, a ghost's state, a
; bomb's fire) -- scenario tests of the rules, where the golden frames
; (tests/2d, tests/3d) check the pixels. See Unit_games.ml.
;
; A game's source can't be linked as is: its last line,
;   let main = Playground_platform.run_app app
; runs the game when the module is initialized. So each game is copied
; here with that line turned into a function, never called:
;   let main () = Playground_platform.run_app app
; (the games themselves unchanged; see notes_debugging_techniques.md
; section 9 for the same trick done by hand).

(rule
 (target TinySokoban.ml)
 (deps (:src %{project_root}/games/TinySokoban.ml))
 (action (with-stdout-to %{target} (run sed "s/^let main =/let main () =/" %{src}))))

(rule
 (target TinyPacman.ml)
 (deps (:src %{project_root}/games/TinyPacman.ml))
 (action (with-stdout-to %{target} (run sed "s/^let main =/let main () =/" %{src}))))

(rule
 (target TinyBomberman.ml)
